WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.280
 There are so many
variables in cooking,

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.050
it's always about
time and temperature.

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:05.260
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:06.764
Any recipe that
you read is going

00:00:06.764 --> 00:00:08.430
to talk about how
long to cook something

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.054
and what temperature
to cook something.

00:00:10.054 --> 00:00:11.740
Remember, they're
only guidelines.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.890
It's really about being
able to appreciate

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:17.140
the technique and the
process and work with it.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:19.440
If you make a mistake, it's OK.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.270
Before you know
it, you'll know how

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:24.240
to roast a beautiful
chicken, pan roast a duck

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.330
breast with crispy skin,
or any things that we've

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.455
been teaching.

00:00:28.455 --> 00:00:30.870
Let's get started.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.580
Young culinarians
ask me all the time

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.300
if I can give them
some words of wisdom,

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.050
and I always give them two.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:38.100
Be patient, and
then be persistent.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.422
Don't let anybody tell you
you can't do something.

00:00:40.422 --> 00:00:41.898
You can.

00:00:41.898 --> 00:00:45.700
What flavor do you really want
in your vegetables or meats?

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.400
It's really up to you.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.845
Don't take anything as a rule.

00:00:50.845 --> 00:00:54.210
In this MasterClass, I'm
very excited to elevate

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:57.300
your cooking abilities.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.420
Super tender.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.160
Look at this dinner.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.660
I love this kind of cooking.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:02.380
To see it.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:02.950
To smell it.

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:03.658
To experience it.

00:01:03.658 --> 00:01:04.800
To hear it.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.450
It truly is transformational,
and it requires,

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:10.080
really a commitment in time.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.730
But if you want to
make great food,

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.520
this is what you have to do.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:19.150
And remember, patience,
patience, patience.

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:25.030
Oh, look at that!

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:28.300
I want you to think about
what you want to be eating.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:31.636
There are so many flavors,
textures, techniques

00:01:31.636 --> 00:01:32.572
and recipes.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:37.200
Simple perfection.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.760
I'm Thomas Keller, and
this is my MasterClass.

